  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{6}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{6}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{2}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFind $\\text{E}[10X+8Y].$",
